  "operative_text": "Section 27573 (Penal Code): (a) A state officer or employee, or operator, lessee, or licensee of any state property, shall not contract for, authorize, or allow the sale of any firearm, firearm precursor part, or ammunition on state property or in the buildings that sit on state property or property otherwise owned, leased, occupied, or operated by the state.\nSection 27573 (Penal Code): (b) This section does not apply to any of the following:\nSection 27573 (Penal Code): (1) A gun buyback event held by a law enforcement agency.\nSection 27573 (Penal Code): (3) The sale of a firearm, firearm precursor part, or ammunition on state property that occurs pursuant to a contract that was entered into before January 1, 2023."
